HostMot2 Ethernet software regression tests
==========================================

Includes the production hm2_eth.c with mock socket send/receive callbacks.
No hardware, network traffic, firewall changes or realtime privileges are used.
Run after configuring/building a run-in-place tree:

    scripts/rip-environment runtests tests/hostmot2/eth
    SANITIZERS=address,undefined bash tests/hostmot2/eth/test.sh

CC can select another C compiler. Sanitizers are optional.
Checks cover transfer sizes -8..520, short/failed reads and writes, unchanged
destinations after failed reads, queue limits, response-buffer bounds,
trailer reservation, queue cleanup and receive rejection after failed sends,
soft-error limits, user error reset, and a successful queued retry.
They do not simulate FPGA timing, hardware recovery, or board discovery.

Hardware validation remains pending. With outputs safely disabled, record
the exact commit, board/firmware, HAL configuration, servo period and results:

- Normal cyclic reads/writes on an Ethernet Mesa board (e.g. 7i96S), including
  a configuration with large TRAM traffic.
- Controlled network interruption, error reporting, recovery and restart.
- 7i95 connector labels (P1/TB1) against the board and firmware.
- PktUART/hm2_modbus traffic if that hardware is available.

These mocks establish host-side bounds and failure behavior, not hardware
compatibility or realtime performance.
